window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-4c6493ddd6abfcda"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prepare-a-leadership-reporting-pack\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">准备领导层汇报材料</h1> <p>把公司进展、财务指标和负责人更新整理成有来源依据的汇报材料。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供上一版汇报材料、进展提纲、计划跟踪表、KPI 和预测输入、领导层笔记及负责人说明，然后请它制作可编辑的公司或董事会更新材料，清晰串联主线、经验证的依据、风险、里程碑和待复核事项。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>使用稳定模板编制的周期性公司、领导层、CFO 或董事会更新。</li> <li>结合项目进展、指标、图表、叙述和负责人输入的汇报周期。</li> <li>需要清楚记录数据变化、风险、下一阶段里程碑和未解决假设的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>更新可编辑的 PowerPoint 演示文稿，保留其视觉规范，并渲染幻灯片以检查版式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>根据最新预测、KPI 和现金来源文件核验更新后的指标与差异。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>从指定的 Drive 位置读取已批准的往期汇报材料、进展跟踪表、预测文件、仪表板、领导层笔记和负责人输入。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取经批准的负责人更新和未解决问题讨论串，为汇报材料提供依据。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>准备汇报材料</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 $slides 和 $spreadsheets，为 [company, leadership, CFO, or board] 准备 [period or topic] 的汇报材料。\n\n请使用我提供的上一版汇报材料或进展提纲、项目跟踪表、指标快照、最新预测模型、KPI 仪表板、现金情况、领导层笔记、负责人说明和待解决问题。如果任何来源位于已连接的插件中，只使用我指定的确切 @google-drive 文件或 @slack 讨论串。\n\n找出各项工作之间的主线，然后更新叙述、依据、关键指标、差异、图表、风险和下一阶段里程碑，同时保留现有演示文稿的视觉规范。请返回可编辑的 .pptx 文件，以及一份简短的汇报摘要，说明改了什么、哪些数据与来源对不上、哪些内容仍需负责人提供、哪些假设尚未解决，以及哪些幻灯片需要领导层审阅。渲染演示文稿，并在交付前修复内容裁切、溢出或版式问题。不要分享文件。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-business-operations-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：业务运营团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"build-the-narrative-from-the-reporting-record\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">根据汇报记录梳理主线</h2> <p>公司和董事会汇报需要一条清晰主线，把项目进展、财务与运营指标、风险和后续步骤串联起来。ChatGPT 可以利用上一版汇报材料组织内容，根据已批准的来源文件提供事实，同时保留演示文稿的视觉规范，并明确显示尚未解决的假设。</p> <p><a id=\"refresh-from-approved-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">根据已批准的来源更新材料</h2> <p>提供上一版汇报材料或进展提纲、项目跟踪表、最新预测、KPI 仪表板、现金情况、领导层笔记和负责人说明。告诉 ChatGPT 哪些幻灯片属于本次范围、哪些来源具有权威性，以及模板中哪些部分必须保持不变。</p> <ol> <li>附上上一版汇报材料和最新的已批准来源文件。</li> <li>说明汇报期间、受众、纳入范围的工作流以及负责审阅的人员。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 梳理进展、依据、风险和下一阶段里程碑之间的主线。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，并要求生成可编辑的 <code>.pptx</code> 文件。</li> <li>核对每项变更后的主张、指标和图表是否能追溯到来源。</li> <li>检查渲染后的幻灯片是否存在裁切、溢出或版式偏移，然后在同一聊天中补齐负责人输入。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"review-what-changed\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">审查变更内容</h2> <p>汇报材料应让人容易区分已更新的事实和仍待回答的问题。请 ChatGPT 在演示文稿旁边保留变更摘要和负责人检查清单，这样审阅者就能关注重要差异，而不必重写整份更新。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Audit the refreshed reporting pack against the prior pack and source files.\n\nList:\n\n- slides with changed metrics, charts, or commentary\n- claims, proof points, risks, and milestone dates that need verification\n- figures that tie to the forecast, KPI dashboard, or cash view\n- figures that do not have a clear source\n- assumptions and owner inputs that remain open\n- slides that need leadership review\n- clipping, overflow, or inconsistent formatting found in the rendered deck\n\nFix safe layout issues, but do not invent or silently replace missing claims or metrics. Keep unresolved items grouped by owner.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请对照上一版汇报材料和来源文件，审查更新后的汇报材料。\n\n列出：\n\n- 指标、图表或说明发生变化的幻灯片\n- 需要核实的主张、佐证、风险和里程碑日期\n- 与预测、KPI 仪表板或现金情况相对应的数字\n- 没有明确来源的数字\n- 尚未确定的假设和负责人输入\n- 需要领导层审阅的幻灯片\n- 渲染后的演示文稿中发现的裁切、溢出或格式不一致问题\n\n修复可以安全处理的版式问题，但不要编造或悄悄替换缺失的主张或指标。按负责人归类保留尚未解决的事项。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"prepare-a-leadership-reporting-pack\">Prepare a leadership reporting pack</h1> <p>Turn company progress, financial metrics, and owner updates into a source-backed reporting pack.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT the prior pack, progress outline, initiative trackers, KPI and forecast inputs, leadership notes, and owner commentary, then ask it to build an editable company or board update with a clear through-line, validated proof points, risks, milestones, and review flags.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Recurring company, leadership, CFO, or board updates built from a stable template.</li> <li>Reporting cycles that combine initiative progress, metrics, charts, narrative, and owner inputs.</li> <li>Teams that need a clear record of changed figures, risks, next milestones, and unresolved assumptions.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$slides</code></td> <td>Update an editable PowerPoint deck, preserve its visual system, and render slides for layout review.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Validate updated metrics and deltas against the latest forecast, KPI, and cash source files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved prior packs, progress trackers, forecast files, dashboards, leadership notes, and owner inputs from exact Drive locations.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved owner updates and open-question threads that should inform the pack.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Prepare the reporting pack</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $slides and $spreadsheets to prepare the [company, leadership, CFO, or board] reporting pack for [period or topic].\n\nUse the prior pack or progress outline, initiative trackers, metric snapshots, latest forecast model, KPI dashboard, cash view, leadership notes, owner commentary, and open questions I provide. If any sources are in connected plugins, use only the exact @google-drive files or @slack threads I name.\n\nIdentify the through-line across workstreams, then update the narrative, proof points, key metrics, deltas, charts, risks, and next milestones while preserving the existing deck's visual system. Return an editable .pptx file and a short pack summary covering what changed, which figures do not tie to a source, what still needs owner input, which assumptions remain open, and which slides need leadership review. Render the deck and fix clipping, overflow, or layout issues before delivery. Do not share it.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-business-operations-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Business operations teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"build-the-narrative-from-the-reporting-record\">Build the narrative from the reporting record</h2> <p>Company and board reporting needs a narrative that connects initiative progress, financial and operating metrics, risks, and next steps. ChatGPT can use the prior pack for structure and approved source files for facts while preserving the deck's visual system and keeping unresolved assumptions visible.</p> <h2 id=\"refresh-from-approved-sources\">Refresh from approved sources</h2> <p>Provide the prior pack or progress outline, initiative trackers, latest forecast, KPI dashboard, cash view, leadership notes, and owner commentary. Tell ChatGPT which slides are in scope, which sources are authoritative, and which parts of the template must remain unchanged.</p> <ol> <li>Attach the prior pack and the latest approved source files.</li> <li>Identify the reporting period, audience, in-scope workstreams, and review owners.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to find the through-line across progress, proof points, risks, and next milestones.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and request an editable <code>.pptx</code> file.</li> <li>Review the source tie-out for every changed claim, metric, and chart.</li> <li>Inspect the rendered slides for clipping, overflow, and layout drift, then resolve owner inputs in the same chat.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"review-what-changed\">Review what changed</h2> <p>The reporting pack should make it easy to distinguish updated facts from open questions. Ask ChatGPT to keep a change summary and owner checklist alongside the deck so reviewers can focus on material differences without rewriting the whole update.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Audit the refreshed reporting pack against the prior pack and source files.\n\nList:\n\n- slides with changed metrics, charts, or commentary\n- claims, proof points, risks, and milestone dates that need verification\n- figures that tie to the forecast, KPI dashboard, or cash view\n- figures that do not have a clear source\n- assumptions and owner inputs that remain open\n- slides that need leadership review\n- clipping, overflow, or inconsistent formatting found in the rendered deck\n\nFix safe layout issues, but do not invent or silently replace missing claims or metrics. Keep unresolved items grouped by owner.\n</code></pre>"};
